WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:20.501
"Hey!" Nathan yelled, rushing after Nora as she tiptoed across their yard.

2
00:00:20.502 --> 00:00:24.682
"What are you doing? Why'd you climb out that window?"

3
00:00:24.683 --> 00:00:30.453
"Come on," Henry said to Cole and Maggie. "Let's catch up to them."

4
00:00:30.454 --> 00:00:34.700
The Lemonade Detectives ran across the yard after Nathan.

5
00:00:34.701 --> 00:00:39.241
By the time they reached him, Nora had stopped and spun around.

6
00:00:39.242 --> 00:00:41.548
She glared at her brother.

7
00:00:41.549 --> 00:00:45.682
"It's none of your business!" she yelled at him.

8
00:00:45.683 --> 00:00:51.173
"Where were you going?" Cole asked Nora, glancing around the yard.

9
00:00:51.174 --> 00:00:57.420
Henry looked around too. Nathan and Nora's backyard was really nice.

10
00:00:57.421 --> 00:01:02.732
There was a big maple tree in the middle where Nathan and his dad had built a tree house.

11
00:01:02.733 --> 00:01:07.854
On the left there was a short picket fence between their yard and the one next door.

12
00:01:07.855 --> 00:01:12.356
A tall hedge on the right blocked the view of the other neighbors' house.

13
00:01:12.357 --> 00:01:17.131
There were no neighbors at all at the back of the yard, just a thick forest.

14
00:01:17.132 --> 00:01:21.891
Henry was pretty sure Nora was headed there when they'd caught her.

15
00:01:21.892 --> 00:01:26.304
"Yeah," he said. "Where were you going, Nora?"

16
00:01:26.305 --> 00:01:30.292
Nora stared at Henry, then at each of the others.

17
00:01:30.293 --> 00:01:34.481
She looked suspicious. "Who wants to know?"

18
00:01:34.482 --> 00:01:39.061
"The Lemonade Detectives, that's who," Maggie replied.

19
00:01:39.062 --> 00:01:41.442
"We want to know what you're up to!"

20
00:01:41.443 --> 00:01:49.464
Henry winced. He didn't think it was a very good idea to tell Nora that they were investigating her.

21
00:01:49.465 --> 00:01:54.803
But Maggie was impulsive. She often spoke before she thought.

22
00:01:54.804 --> 00:01:59.706
Nora stared at them all again. For a second she didn't answer.

23
00:01:59.707 --> 00:02:02.490
"Well?" Nathan demanded.

24
00:02:02.491 --> 00:02:07.613
"I was just walking across the backyard," Nora said at last.

25
00:02:07.614 --> 00:02:09.637
"What's wrong with that?"

26
00:02:09.638 --> 00:02:13.891
"Why did you climb out the playroom window instead of using the door?"

27
00:02:13.892 --> 00:02:19.678
Nathan pointed to the back door of their house. "It's right there, you know!"

28
00:02:19.679 --> 00:02:22.528
"I was in a hurry," Nora said.

29
00:02:22.529 --> 00:02:26.923
"I, um, saw a butterfly and I wanted to catch it."

30
00:02:26.924 --> 00:02:29.128
Henry glanced at Cole.

31
00:02:29.129 --> 00:02:35.310
He could tell his friend was thinking the same thing he was. Nora was lying.

32
00:02:35.311 --> 00:02:38.948
But how were they supposed to get her to tell the truth now?

33
00:02:38.949 --> 00:02:41.463
She knew they were watching her.

34
00:02:41.464 --> 00:02:45.531
That was going to make their job as detectives much harder.

35
00:02:45.532 --> 00:02:51.747
"It's okay, Nora," Henry said. "Go ahead and do whatever you were doing."

36
00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:54.845
"I wasn't doing anything," Nora said.

37
00:02:54.846 --> 00:02:57.847
"I was just about to go back inside."

38
00:02:57.848 --> 00:03:01.957
She ran over and climbed back inside through the window.

39
00:03:01.958 --> 00:03:04.285
Maggie stared after her.

40
00:03:04.286 --> 00:03:11.788
"You were right," she told Nathan. "She is acting even weirder than usual."

41
00:03:11.789 --> 00:03:15.437
Cole shrugged. "So what do we do now?

42
00:03:15.438 --> 00:03:18.530
She didn't seem very eager to tell us anything."

43
00:03:18.531 --> 00:03:23.354
"We'll have to figure out what's going on in a different way," Henry said.

44
00:03:23.355 --> 00:03:27.962
"Maybe we should try a stakeout," Maggie suggested.

45
00:03:27.963 --> 00:03:31.146
"That worked last time we were suspicious of her."

46
00:03:31.147 --> 00:03:33.552
"No it didn't," Cole said.

47
00:03:33.553 --> 00:03:37.418
"Last time we staked out Nora's house, she turned out to be innocent."

48
00:03:37.419 --> 00:03:41.365
"True, but Maggie's right," Henry said.

49
00:03:41.366 --> 00:03:46.641
"If we hide and wait for Nora to sneak out again, we'll be able to follow her.

50
00:03:46.642 --> 00:03:50.405
Then we can see where she's going and what she's doing."

51
00:03:50.406 --> 00:03:54.141
"You mean we have to sit around here all day?"

52
00:03:54.142 --> 00:03:58.601
Maggie suddenly didn't look very happy about the stakeout idea.

53
00:03:58.602 --> 00:04:01.295
"What about my lemonade stand?"

54
00:04:01.296 --> 00:04:07.274
Henry glanced at Nathan. "You said she's been sneaking out at night, right?"

55
00:04:07.275 --> 00:04:10.306
"Sort of," Nathan said.

56
00:04:10.307 --> 00:04:15.668
"Her bedtime is at seven, so it's not usually very late when she sneaks out."

57
00:04:15.669 --> 00:04:23.079
"Perfect." Henry smiled. "All we have to do is come back at seven and wait!"

58
00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:30.340
That evening at exactly seven o'clock, The Lemonade Detectives met behind the hedge along Nora's yard.

59
00:04:30.341 --> 00:04:33.084
Nathan was waiting for them there.

60
00:04:33.085 --> 00:04:38.240
"Perfect timing," he whispered. "Nora just went to bed."

61
00:04:38.241 --> 00:04:42.022
Henry nodded. He peeked through the hedge.

62
00:04:42.023 --> 00:04:46.089
It hid them from view, but allowed them to see Nora's house.

63
00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:50.440
"Does she usually sneak out the back door?" he asked.

64
00:04:50.441 --> 00:04:53.446
"She used to," Nathan replied.

65
00:04:53.447 --> 00:04:57.557
"But Mom and Dad started locking it once all this started."

66
00:04:57.558 --> 00:05:01.642
"Maybe she'll climb out the playroom window again," Cole said.

67
00:05:01.643 --> 00:05:06.864
Nathan nodded. "Or she might use her bedroom window," he said.

68
00:05:06.865 --> 00:05:11.403
"It's upstairs, but she knows how to climb down the house.

69
00:05:11.404 --> 00:05:14.985
It's part of our family's fire-safety plan."

70
00:05:14.986 --> 00:05:19.116
"Okay, let's watch both windows," Henry said.

71
00:05:19.117 --> 00:05:22.556
They all settled down behind the hedge to wait.

72
00:05:22.557 --> 00:05:25.147
But they didn't have to wait very long.

73
00:05:25.148 --> 00:05:29.369
About twenty minutes later, they heard a window slide open.

74
00:05:29.370 --> 00:05:35.257
Maggie peeked through the hedge. "It's Nora!" she whispered.

75
00:05:35.258 --> 00:05:38.769
"She's climbing out her bedroom window."

76
00:05:38.770 --> 00:05:40.777
Henry looked too.

77
00:05:40.778 --> 00:05:45.268
He saw Nora climb out her bedroom window and jump to the ground.

78
00:05:45.269 --> 00:05:49.264
She glanced around, and then scurried across the yard.

79
00:05:49.265 --> 00:05:53.946
"She sure doesn't look like she's sleepwalking," Henry whispered.

80
00:05:53.947 --> 00:05:58.698
"Come on, let's follow her!"
